    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d552">

                <pb facs="0561" n="551" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg551"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/3429b</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of the American
                        Republics</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Duggan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Haitian Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lescot</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-07">August 7, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: In accordance with your
                    request for a brief statement of the policy and attitude of this Government with
                    respect to the matters which we have recently been discussing, I take pleasure
                    in sending you herewith a brief memorandum which I hope is adequate for your
                    purposes.</p>
                <p>I am hopeful that prior to your departure from Washington further information
                    will have been received from our Embassy in Paris with regard to the 1910
                    Haitian franc loan. If such information is received I shall, of course,
                    communicate with you at once.</p>
                <p>I am, my dear Mr. Lescot,</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Laurence Duggan</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d552-a1.xml" xpointer="d552-a1"/>
            </div>
